# Story 19: Stacked Panes (45s)
# Hook: Stack panes like a deck of cards -- many terminals in the footprint of one.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-019-stacked-panes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Stack panes like a deck of cards -- many terminals in the footprint of one.

[00:04.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh with a single pane.

[00:09.0 --> 00:17.0]
Press Ctrl+P then s to stack a new pane on top of the group. The border title now reads one of two.

[00:17.0 --> 00:25.0]
Stack another and the title shows one of three. Only the front pane is full-size.

[00:25.0 --> 00:35.0]
The panes behind it sit in the same slot, showing up as grey title bars at the bottom -- a deck you flip through.

[00:35.0 --> 00:45.0]
Stacking keeps related terminals together without crowding your screen. Next up: rotating through the stack.

